{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/numberofspanningtrees(weight:)-28jjs"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/numberOfSpanningTrees(weight:)-28jjs"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of spanning trees τ(G), weighted: the sum over spanning trees of the product of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their weights, which is any cofactor of the Laplacian (Kirchhoff’s matrix-tree theorem)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Loops never lie on a tree; parallel edges each count. 0 for the empty graph and for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disconnected one, 1 for one vertex. NetworkX "},{"code":"number_of_spanning_trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:SB"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":": counts pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" quickly (K₂₅ has 25²³). A dense Cholesky factorization of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Laplacian with one vertex removed, its pivots multiplied with the binary exponent kept apart,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the result overflows only past "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"’s range, to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".infinity"},{"type":"text","text":". When every weight is an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integer (unweighted included) a result below 2⁵³ is rounded to the nearest integer, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then exact; nearer to 2⁵³ and above, it is within a relative 10⁻¹² or so, not exact. O(n³) time,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every weight is finite and nonnegative.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"numberOfSpanningTrees(weight:)","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE21numberOfSpanningTrees6weightSdqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_tSBRd__lF","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"numberOfSpanningTrees","kind":"ident